# Sparse runoff package parameters (pkg/rnf)
#
# The same runoff as the dense case input.rnof_yearly, in sparse form:
# one file per year, runoff_sparse_1978.nc and
# runoff_sparse_1979.nc, 365 daily records each, the first
# at 1 January 00:00. RNF_useYearlyFiles is the one setting
# a sparse file cannot carry itself, so data.rnf gives it;
# RNF_file is the base name and the reader reads
# <base>_YYYY.nc.
#
# The file is written by ../input.rnof_const/gen_sparse.py from the
# dense records of input.rnof_yearly and is read from that directory,
# so both cases force the model with the same runoff. Apart from
# RNF_useYearlyFiles, every timing value the reader needs comes from
# the time axis of the file, which is what this case checks; data.rnf
# overrides none of them.
 &RNF_PARM01
  RNF_file = '../input.rnof_yearly/runoff_sparse.nc',
  RNF_useYearlyFiles = .TRUE.,
 &
